## .NET
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.user
.vs/
artifacts/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

## App runtime data
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
# File logging (TenonAdmin:Logging:File, off by default); no leading slash → matches logs/ under any host
logs/
# A pattern with an internal slash gets anchored to the repo root; only a **/ prefix matches upload dirs
# under any host (e.g. samples/*/wwwroot)
**/wwwroot/upload/

## Backend local dev config (contains seed credentials, not committed; use the .example template + dotnet user-secrets)
backend/**/appsettings.Development.json

## Frontend (web/)
node_modules/
dist/
.env.local
# Playwright artifacts: web/.gitignore already ignores the same-named dirs under web/, but running from the repo root misses these
test-results/
playwright-report/

## Tooling / agent state (local tooling artifacts, not committed; no leading slash → matches at any depth, incl. backend/.omc)
.omc/
.omx/
.codegraph/
# Local Claude Code hook scripts: only take effect when referenced by .claude/settings.json, which is likewise not committed,
# so committing this alone would be pointless.
# If we ever want every collaborator to get some hook (e.g. "version numbers may only be written into Directory.Packages.props"),
# hooks/ and settings.json need to be committed together — unignore this line at that point.
.claude/hooks/
.claude/launch.json
.claude/settings.local.json

## Backend scratch/verification scripts
backend/scratchpad/

## dev scripts (mac/linux) runtime
.dev/

## Sync-tool conflict copies / transfer temp files (generated by Syncthing etc., local junk files)
*.sync-conflict-*
~syncthing~*
